      "title": "JEE Advanced 2023 (Paper 2)"
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>&nbsp;denote the base of the natural logarithm. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>e</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ujsad",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TWBee",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UbvOf",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CKY5",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now differentiating both side we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Which is a linear differential equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Now solution is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now using given value,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>e</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>e</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>",
